sg-shell (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Control Panel, rebuilt as a real one (src/control/): the Windows 10
    category view, category pages, All Control Panel Items with search, and a
    navigation bar (back, forward, up, breadcrumb). Applets, all live:
    - System: edition, build, hardware, computer name, domain or workgroup,
      account type; "Change settings" renames the computer or joins a domain.
    - Programs and Features: every Uninstall entry (both registry views and
      the user's), as Windows filters them; Uninstall / Change / Repair run the
      program's own commands (msiexec for Windows Installer products).
    - User Accounts: your account; manage local accounts -- create, change
      type, reset password, delete (keep or delete files).
    - Date and Time: clock, Windows and IANA zone, next daylight-saving
      change, Internet time; change the zone and time synchronisation.
    - Personalization: desktop picture (JPEG/PNG/BMP, all six fits), solid
      color, accent color, light/dark app and Windows modes -- in Windows'
      own registry values, applied live.
    - Windows Update: status, last check, restart to install, sources, apt
      history; "Check for updates".
    - Network and Sharing Center: active networks and adapters (read-only;
      Network Connections is sg-ncpa's).
    - Hosted .cpl applets (Internet Options, Game Controllers, Display, and
      any third party's) through CPlApplet.
    control.exe's .cpl names, keywords and /name Microsoft.* names open the
    matching applet.
  * sg-admind: the Control Panel's privileged half. Elevated (SYSTEM) copies
    of the Control Panel file requests in a spool only SYSTEM can write;
    sg-admind.path runs the root service, which acts on a fixed, validated
    list of operations. Gated by test/admind-check.sh.
  * Default fonts: ClearType, Segoe UI 9 pt as Inter, metric-compatible
    stand-ins (from the main theming work).

